        You are a programming expert. 
        You will be provided with a patch used to fix a bug. 
        Based on the commit message and modifications in the patch, you need to analyze the root cause of the bug in detail. 

        Here is the patch content:
        From bf21861e89e50caad342043d4dcffdd30d5e9434 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ned Twigg <ned.twigg@diffplug.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Dec 2016 18:11:25 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] Fixed unused imports, and fixed a bug I introduced in
 7434506f7fd3a069f899c1d535eaf0a876306c6f.

---
 src/main/java/com/diffplug/gradle/oomph/ConventionJdt.java | 4 +---
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/main/java/com/diffplug/gradle/oomph/ConventionJdt.java b/src/main/java/com/diffplug/gradle/oomph/ConventionJdt.java
index 9cf914d..b1502b8 100644
--- a/src/main/java/com/diffplug/gradle/oomph/ConventionJdt.java
+++ b/src/main/java/com/diffplug/gradle/oomph/ConventionJdt.java
@@ -16,9 +16,7 @@
 package com.diffplug.gradle.oomph;

 import java.util.HashSet;
-import java.util.LinkedHashMap;
 import java.util.List;
-import java.util.Map;
 import java.util.Set;

 import org.gradle.api.Action;
@@ -77,7 +75,7 @@ public class ConventionJdt extends OomphConvention {
 				"org.eclipse.jdt.core.compiler.compliance",
 				"org.eclipse.jdt.core.compiler.source");
 		extension.workspaceProp(JDT_CORE_PREFS, props -> {
-			JDT_COMPLIANCE_PROPS.forEach(p -> props.put(p, compilerComplianceLevel.toString()));
+			JDT_COMPLIANCE_PROPS.forEach(p -> props.put(p, JavaVersion.toVersion(compilerComplianceLevel).toString()));
 			//Use default compliance settings.
 			props.put("org.eclipse.jdt.core.compiler.codegen.inlineJsrBytecode", "enabled");
 			props.put("org.eclipse.jdt.core.compiler.problem.assertIdentifier", "error");
-- 
2.25.1



        Provide a response strictly in the following format:
        Root cause:<Root cause>

    You are a programming expert.
    You will be given the root cause of a bug and  the corresponding patch.
    You need to extract the code statements that lead to the bug from  the patch, based on the root cause.


    Provide a response strictly in the following format:
    Code statements:
    <text1>
    <text2>
    <text3>
    <text4>
    ...
    <textN>

Root cause:
The bug was caused by using the `compilerComplianceLevel` directly as a string in the `props.put` method, which did not convert the compliance level to the appropriate Java version format. This led to incorrect values being set in the properties for the JDT compliance settings. The fix involved using `JavaVersion.toVersion(compilerComplianceLevel).toString()` to ensure the compliance level was correctly formatted before being added to the properties.
